      "rev_n_1_fbab35_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_fbab35_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_fbab35",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the jump pattern to find a closed-form formula based on the parity of k, then implement O(1) calculation per query.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507296.3348985
      },
      "rev_n_2_1d16c7_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_1d16c7_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_1d16c7",
        "thought_text": "Simulate the jumps step-by-step for small k to verify the pattern, but realize simulation is too slow for k=10^9, so derive the formula instead.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507296.3349123
      },
      "rev_n_3_3ae257_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_3ae257_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_3ae257",
        "thought_text": "Group jumps into pairs of (a, -b) and calculate the net displacement per pair, handling the remainder if k is odd.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507296.33492
      },
      "rev_n_4_ed26bd_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_ed26bd_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_ed26bd",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the number of full (a, -b) pairs as k // 2, multiply by (a - b), then add 'a' if k is odd.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6628490542968644657",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507315.026854
      },
      "rev_n_5_78720b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_78720b_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_78720b",
        "thought_text": "Determine the number of right jumps (ceil(k/2)) and left jumps (floor(k/2)) separately, then compute (right_jumps * a) - (left_jumps * b).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6628490542968644657",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507315.0268745
      },
      "rev_n_6_a33c71_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_a33c71_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_a33c71",
        "thought_text": "Use modular arithmetic to find the position after k jumps by observing the pattern repeats every 2 jumps, handling the remainder k % 2.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "6628490542968644657",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507315.0268874
      },
      "rev_n_7_19d2bd_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_19d2bd_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_19d2bd",
        "thought_text": "Derive a closed-form formula by observing that every pair of jumps (right then left) results in a net displacement of (a - b). Calculate the number of full pairs as k // 2 and the remainder as k % 2 to handle the final single jump if k is odd.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4434050753594516823",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507323.6289892
      },
      "rev_n_8_30f435_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_30f435_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_30f435",
        "thought_text": "Simulate the process logically without iterating: if k is even, the result is simply (k/2) * (a - b); if k is odd, it is ((k-1)/2) * (a - b) + a. This avoids loops and handles large k efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4434050753594516823",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507323.6290061
      },
      "rev_n_9_ae3d61_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_ae3d61_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_ae3d61",
        "thought_text": "Use integer division and modulo operators directly in the code: result = (k // 2) * (a - b) + (a if k % 2 == 1 else 0). This is the most concise O(1) implementation strategy.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "4434050753594516823",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507323.629014
      },
      "rev_n_10_c76c7c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_c76c7c_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_c76c7c",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the jump pattern to find a closed-form formula based on the number of complete pairs of jumps (a - b) and the remainder, avoiding O(k) simulation.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2843127274359567037",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794507332.6060321
      },
      "rev_n_11_abefdb_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_abefdb_0",
